from round4_report import counts

def render(rows):
 from report import GATES
 lines=['# Issue #248 Phase B — Round 6','','**PROVISIONAL on plateau Z24.65 / unmeasured Junana q=1.50. NOT RELEASED.**','','## Round 6 results','','Assignment correction inside the frozen round-3 final framework. Failed gates remain binding; no production release or exception is claimed.','','| Gate | 17 mm | 16 mm |','|---|---|---|']
 lines += [f'| {n} | {rows[17][i]} | {rows[16][i]} |' for i,n in enumerate(GATES)]
 lines += ['', '### Frozen base, physical assignment and exact deviation scope','',
 'The latest PO direction was read with `gh issue view 248 --comments` and is preserved in sources/issue248-round6.json. The entire round-5 package and report are frozen in round5/ with round5-sha256.json; all earlier evidence remains unchanged. Checkpoint 84be3a5 froze round 5 before work began. An initial issue snapshot command used incompatible gh flags and produced an empty file; it was immediately corrected using `gh issue view 248 --json comments` before the geometry checkpoint.', '',
 'BASE is the FINAL round-3 assembly whose 17 mm audit has 80 contacts and whose longest finished conductor is 198.400068 mm. Its stored/released turn-tangent datums are Y10.0/Y−5.1, reserve centre X±17.40, and travel 15.10 mm (connected reserve 30.20 mm). The tuning-round Y17.1/Y2.0 datums are not used. No reserve, lane pack, pack spacing/height, shell, strip, retainer (±8,−30), hardware, tray channel or tray seating relief is redesigned.', '',
 'The frozen round-3 strand geometry DOES exist as parametric paths in round3/routes-round3.json and round3/routes.py, consistent with the frozen measurements. No paths are fitted from solids. Each corrected conductor retains the entire path belonging to its physical Wing outlet, including every inlet waypoint, low-pack radius/height, reserve turn and return-fan waypoint through the last interior vertex. Only the final two Main approach waypoints are taken from the frozen path that terminates at the corrected same-numbered Main cavity. right Wing pin1 is X35.125, pin14 X18.875; left pin1 is X−18.875. Native KiCad pads/nets independently verify all 28 endpoints in pinmap-round6.json against immutable pinmap-round4.json / pinmap-round5.json.', '',
 'The complete deviation register is assignment-deviations-round6.json, naming all 28 conductors (right pin and its mirrored left pin), original physical lane, old/new Main approach coordinates, unchanged waypoint indices and affected geometry. For each strand: after vertices5/6 change; edges4→5 and5→6 and R5 fillets at vertices4/5 regenerate; the tangent trim at unchanged vertex4 on edge3→4 consequently changes. Vertex4 itself does not move. All indices are zero-based. Entire inlet/reserve geometry and preceding fan vertices remain exactly unchanged. routes-round6.json is checked against the frozen arrays by verify_round6_framework.py; there is no route optimizer or extra clearance cut.', '',
 'Frozen solid recovery uses content-addressed byte-identical BReps for 338 fixed constituents, including boards, plates, Fly, strips, retainers and hardware. Only central shell and two tray serialized BReps were absent from scratch; these three operands are read from their immutable final round-3 manufacturing STEP exports without healing. Their representation roundtrip volume/bounds changes are recorded individually in frozen-framework-recovery.json. This is solid recovery, not path reconstruction or a new shape design. The first partial 17 mm attempt exposed whole-assembly reserialization by the legacy boss-repair writer; it was stopped after a bounded chunk, retained under .issue248-runtime/round6/rejected-operand-reserialization/, and replaced with a writer that changes only tray-left. Its partial pair results are not reused. Independent final scope checks reject any change beyond the strand edits and carried tray-left repair.', '',
 'CARRIED manufacturing-data repair: fresh analytic OD7 tray-left splice boss at X0/Y55 with original Ø1.7 pilot; explicit X−4…4/Y51…59/Z1.8…5.8 cleanup, native floor patch restored through Z1.6…2.0. splice-boss-rebuild.json records exact before/after volume and floor preservation. No other tray relief is cut, including no continuous-service or corrected-route channel enlargement. Required skin, source floor, full E supports, palm band and stack checks remain unchanged.', '',
 'The minimum terminal-only correction exceeds the finished-length limit. The >200 mm route is preserved for an exact audit and a failed gate; no routing shortening, tail reduction, reserve shift or waiver is substituted. Binding thresholds remain deck Z13.55, plateau Z24.65/q1.50 provisional, seam ownership and 2.00 mm skin, byte-unchanged board/plate design inputs, GH/Fly blisters, M2×10, fourteen OD1/R≥5 strands per side, finished ≤200 mm including unchanged 3.90/3.40 mm tails, Fly 170/R5/0.30 gap, and 1e−6 mm³ collision threshold.', '']
 for pitch in (17,16):
  out=HERE/f'{pitch}mm';get=lambda n:read(out/(n+'.json'));a=get('audit');lf=get('length-fly');s=get('service');v=get('export-verification');ret=get('retention-check');skin=get('tuning-blockers')
  olds=[read(HERE/f'round{r}/{pitch}mm/audit.json') for r in (3,4,5)];cc=[counts(q['unexpected_interferences']) for q in olds+[a]]
  pairs=lambda audit:{tuple(sorted((h['a'],h['b']))) for h in audit['unexpected_interferences']}
  comparisons=[]
  for rd,old_a,old_counts in zip((3,4,5),olds,cc):
   comparisons.append(dict(round=rd,baseline_audit_sha256=sha(HERE/f'round{rd}/{pitch}mm/audit.json'),categories={n:dict(baseline=old_counts[n],round6=cc[3][n]) for n in sorted(set(old_counts)|set(cc[3]))},cleared_named_pairs=sorted(pairs(old_a)-pairs(a)),remaining_named_pairs=sorted(pairs(old_a)&pairs(a)),new_named_pairs=sorted(pairs(a)-pairs(old_a))))
  save(out/'round6-comparison.json',dict(geometry_sha256=sha(out/'assembly-index.json'),baselines=comparisons))
